What is the Python code that can extract the top 5 rated romantic comedy movies from an online movie database API? The code must use the 'genre' and 'rating' parameters to narrow down the search results. Once the movies are extracted, the code should display their titles, ratings, and plot summaries.
Here is the JSON data that can be used:
{
 "results": [
 {
 "title": "Crazy Rich Asians",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 7.5,
 "summary": "This contemporary romantic comedy, based on a global bestseller, follows native New Yorker Rachel Chu to Singapore to meet her boyfriend's family."
 },
 {
 "title": "To All the Boys I've Loved Before",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 7.1,
 "summary": "A teenage girl's secret love letters are exposed and wreak havoc on her love life."
 },
 {
 "title": "Isn't It Romantic",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 5.9,
 "summary": "A young woman disenchanted with love mysteriously finds herself trapped inside a romantic comedy."
 },
 {
 "title": "The Big Sick",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 7.5,
 "summary": "Pakistan-born comedian Kumail Nanjiani and grad student Emily Gardner fall in love but struggle as their cultures clash."
 },
 {
 "title": "Set It Up",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 6.5,
 "summary": "Two overworked assistants hatch a plan to make their bosses fall in love."
 }
 ]
}
Here is the Python code that can extract the top 5 rated romantic comedy movies:
import json
data = '''
{
 "results": [
 {
 "title": "Crazy Rich Asians",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 7.5,
 "summary": "This contemporary romantic comedy, based on a global bestseller, follows native New Yorker Rachel Chu to Singapore to meet her boyfriend's family."
 },
 {
 "title": "To All the Boys I've Loved Before",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 7.1,
 "summary": "A teenage girl's secret love letters are exposed and wreak havoc on her love life."
 },
 {
 "title": "Isn't It Romantic",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 5.9,
 "summary": "A young woman disenchanted with love mysteriously finds herself trapped inside a romantic comedy."
 },
 {
 "title": "The Big Sick",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 7.5,
 "summary": "Pakistan-born comedian Kumail Nanjiani and grad student Emily Gardner fall in love but struggle as their cultures clash."
 },
 {
 "title": "Set It Up",
 "genre": "Romantic Comedy",
 "rating": 6.5,
 "summary": "Two overworked assistants hatch a plan to make their bosses fall in love."
 }
 ]
}'''
movies = json.loads(data)['results']
romantic_comedies = [movie for movie in movies if movie['genre'] == 'Romantic Comedy']
top_five = sorted(romantic_comedies, key=lambda movie: movie['rating'], reverse=True)[:5]
for movie in top_five:
 print(f"Title: {movie['title']}nRating: {movie['rating']}nSummary: {movie['summary']}n")
<|end|>
