Certainly! The Nile River is the longest river in the world, stretching over 4,000 miles from its source in Burundi to its mouth at the Mediterranean Sea. The river passes through 11 countries in total, including:
1. Burundi
2. Rwanda
3. Tanzania
4. Uganda
5. Kenya
6. Democratic Republic of the Congo
7. South Sudan
8. Sudan
9. Egypt
10. Eritrea
