<|user|>
What Go code can I use to create a vegan and gluten-free pasta dish using ingredients commonly found in a college dorm room?
Here are the steps to follow:
1. Cook pasta according to package directions.
2. In a separate pan, heat olive oil and sauté diced onions and minced garlic.
3. Add sliced mushrooms and cook until tender.
4. Stir in canned diced tomatoes and a splash of vegetable broth.
5. Season with salt, pepper, and Italian seasoning to taste.
6. Once the pasta is cooked, drain and add it to the sauce pan.
7. Toss to coat the pasta in the sauce.
8. Serve topped with chopped fresh parsley and a sprinkle of nutritional yeast.
Here is the Go code for the recipe:
package main
import (
 "fmt"
)
func main() {
 fmt.Println("Vegan and Gluten-Free Pasta Recipe")
 fmt.Println("Ingredients:")
 fmt.Println("- Pasta")
 fmt.Println("- Olive oil")
 fmt.Println("- Onion")
 fmt.Println("- Garlic")
 fmt.Println("- Mushrooms")
 fmt.Println("- Canned diced tomatoes")
 fmt.Println("- Vegetable broth")
 fmt.Println("- Salt")
 fmt.Println("- Pepper")
 fmt.Println("- Italian seasoning")
 fmt.Println("- Fresh parsley")
 fmt.Println("- Nutritional yeast")
 fmt.Println("nInstructions:")
 fmt.Println("1. Cook pasta according to package directions.")
 fmt.Println("2. In a separate pan, heat olive oil and sauté diced onions and minced garlic.")
 fmt.Println("3. Add sliced mushrooms and cook until tender.")
 fmt.Println("4. Stir in canned diced tomatoes and a splash of vegetable broth.")
