What Swift code can be used to fetch and display the top 10 websites that have significantly contributed to the growth and development of the internet, along with a brief explanation of their impact on society, in an HTML page?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To fetch and display the top 10 websites that have significantly contributed to the growth and development of the internet, you can use Swift's URLSession and HTML parsing libraries. Here's an example code snippet that fetches the top 10 websites from a website and displays them in an HTML page:
```swift
import Foundation
import SwiftSoup
let urlString = "https://www.makeuseof.com/tag/most-important-websites-internet/"
let url = URL(string: urlString)!
let task = URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: url) { (data, response, error) in
 if let error = error {
 print("Error: (error)")
 return
 }
 
 guard let data = data else {
 print("No data returned from server")
 return
 }
 
 do {
 let htmlString = String(data: data, encoding: .utf8)!
 let doc: Document = try SwiftSoup.parse(htmlString)
 
 var websites: [String] = []
 var descriptions: [String] = []
 
 for i in 1...10 {
 let website = try doc.select("h2:nth-of-type((i)) a").text()
 let description = try doc.select("h2:nth-of-type((i)) ~ p").first()?.text() ?? ""
 websites.append(website)
 descriptions.append(description)
 }
 
 var html = ""
 for i in 0..<websites.count {
 html += "<h2>(websites[i])"
 html += "(descriptions[i])

"
 }
 html += ""
 
 print(html)
 } catch {
 print("Error parsing HTML: (error)")
 }
}
task.resume()
```
This code fetches the top 10 websites from a website using URLSession, and then parses the HTML using SwiftSoup. It then extracts the website names and descriptions, and stores them in separate arrays. Finally, it generates an HTML page with the website names and descriptions, and prints it to the console. You can modify this code to display the HTML page in a web view or save it to a file. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
