sin(C) = 3 sin(A) / 15
sin(C) = 0.609
Taking the inverse sine of both sides, we get:
C = 37.4 degrees
Therefore, the internal angle measures of the given triangle with side lengths of 14, 3, and 15 are approximately A = 12.3 degrees, B = 13.2 degrees, and C = 37.4 degrees. <|endoftext|>
