In addition to their graphical representation, vectors can also be described algebraically using coordinates or matrices. This allows us to perform operations on vectors, such as addition, subtraction, and scalar multiplication. By manipulating vectors in this way, we can solve a variety of problems in mathematics and its applications. <|endoftext|>
