What Ruby code can I use to generate a list of books that a 6th grader might enjoy? Can you please provide an example using the following criteria: books with a reading level between 5th and 8th grade, genres include adventure, fantasy, and mystery, and published within the last 10 years. Thank you!
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Here's an example of Ruby code that could generate a list of books that meet the criteria you specified:
```ruby
require 'json'
require 'open-uri'
# Define the search criteria
reading_level = "5-8"
genres = ["adventure", "fantasy", "mystery"]
max_age = 10
# Construct the URL for the API request
url = "https://api.nytimes.com/svc/books/v3/lists.json"
url += "?api-key=YOUR_API_KEY"
url += "&list=middle-grade-hardcover"
url += "&age-group=#{reading_level}"
url += "&sort-by=best-sellers"
url += "&max-age=#{max_age}"
# Make the API request and parse the response
response = open(url).read
data = JSON.parse(response)
# Filter the results based on the specified genres
books = data["results"].select do |book|
 genres.include?(book["display_name"].downcase)
end
# Print the list of books
puts "Here are some books you might enjoy:"
books.each do |book|
 puts "- #{book["book_details"][0]["title"]} by #{book["book_details"][0]["author"]}"
end
```
This code uses the New York Times Books API to search for books that meet the specified criteria. It constructs a URL with the appropriate query parameters and makes a request to the API. It then filters the results based on the specified genres and prints out a list of books that match the criteria.
Note that you'll need to replace `YOUR_API_KEY` in the URL with your actual API key for this code to work. You can get an API key by signing up for the New York Times Developer Network. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That's really helpful, thank you! Can you explain how the API query parameters work in this code?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I'd be happy to. The API query parameters specify the search criteria that the API will use to return a list of books. Here's a breakdown of each parameter:

- `list=middle-grade-hardcover`: This parameter specifies that we want to search for books on the middle grade hardcover bestseller list.
- `age-group=#{reading_level}`: This parameter sets the age group for the search based on the reading level criteria that was defined in the Ruby code. In this case, it will be set to the string "5-8".
- `sort-by=best-sellers`: This parameter sorts the results by best-sellers.
- `max-age=#{max_age}`: This parameter limits the age of the book to be no more than 10-years-old.

By using these parameters, we can ensure that the API only returns books that match our criteria. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


