How can we use Java code to analyze the sea level trends over time and assess the potential impact on coastal communities and the global economy using the given XML data? 
We can start by parsing the XML data using the following Java code:
DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
DocumentBuilder builder = factory.newDocumentBuilder();
Document doc = builder.parse(new InputSource(new StringReader(xmlData)));
doc.getDocumentElement().normalize();
Then, we can extract the sea level data by looping through the "seaLevels" nodes and creating a list of sea level values:
NodeList seaLevels = doc.getElementsByTagName("seaLevels");
List seaLevelValues = new ArrayList<>();
for (int i = 0; i < seaLevels.getLength(); i++) {
 Node seaLevel = seaLevels.item(i);
 if (seaLevel.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {
 Element seaLevelElement = (Element) seaLevel;
 double level = Double.parseDouble(seaLevelElement.getElementsByTagName("level").item(0).getTextContent());
 seaLevelValues.add(level);
 }
}
Next, we can use statistical analysis methods to analyze the sea level trends over time and make predictions about future sea levels. We can also calculate the impact of these sea level changes on coastal communities by looping through the "community" nodes and calculating the total population and coastal length affected by each sea level increase:
NodeList communities = doc.getElementsByTagName("community");
double totalPopulationAffected = 0;
double totalCoastalLengthAffected = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < communities.getLength(); i++) {
 Node community = communities.item(i);
 if (community.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {
 Element communityElement = (Element) community;
 double population = Double.parseDouble(communityElement.getElementsByTagName("population").item(0).getTextContent());
 double coastalLength = Double.parseDouble(communityElement.getElementsByTagName("coastalLength").item(0).getTextContent());
 double seaLevelImpact = Double.parseDouble(communityElement.getElementsByTagName("seaLevelImpact").item(0).getTextContent());
 totalPopulationAffected += population * (seaLevelImpact / 100);
 totalCoastalLengthAffected += coastalLength * (seaLevelImpact / 100);
 }
}
Similarly, we can calculate the impact of sea level changes on different sectors of the global economy by looping through the "sector" nodes and calculating the total impact on each sector:
NodeList sectors = doc.getElementsByTagName("sector");
double totalEconomicImpact = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < sectors.getLength(); i++) {
 Node sector = sectors.item(i);
 if (sector.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {
 Element sectorElement = (Element) sector;
 double impact = Double.parseDouble(sectorElement.getElementsByTagName("impact").item(0).getTextContent().replace("%", ""));
 totalEconomicImpact += impact;
 }
}
With these calculations, we can provide a comprehensive analysis of the effects of climate change on sea levels and its potential impact on coastal communities and the global economy.
