- OrigamiUSA (https://origamiusa.org/) is a great resource for all things origami, including tutorials, diagrams, and information on upcoming events.
- The Origami Resource Center (http://www.origami-resource-center.com/) is another great online resource for origami enthusiasts of all skill levels.
- "Origami Design Secrets" by Robert J. Lang is a highly recommended book for those interested in designing their own origami models.
- YouTube is also a great source for origami tutorials, with channels like "EZ Origami" and "JeremyShaferOrigami" offering step-by-step instructions for a wide variety of models.

I hope these resources help you further explore the fascinating world of origami! <|endoftext|>
