To format Mary's direct speech sentence correctly in a LaTeX document, you can use the textquotedblleft and textquotedblright commands to insert the opening and closing quotation marks, respectively. Additionally, you should include the punctuation inside the closing quotation mark. Here's an example:
```
Mary said, textquotedblleft I love LaTeX!textquotedblright.
```
This will produce the following output:
```
Mary said, "I love LaTeX!".
``` 
Note that the period is inside the closing quotation mark. This is the standard convention for punctuating direct speech in English. <|endoftext|>
