<|user|>
In a LaTeX document, if I want to insert an image, what is the recommended format of the image file?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
When inserting an image in a LaTeX document, it is recommended to use an encapsulated postscript (EPS) or portable document format (PDF) file. These formats are vector-based and can be scaled without losing quality. To insert an image using LaTeX, you can use the graphicx package and the includegraphics command. Here's an example:

```
usepackage{graphicx}
...
begin{figure}
 centering
 includegraphics[width=0.5textwidth]{image.eps}
 caption{Caption for the image.}
 label{fig:image}
end{figure}
```

This will insert the image "image.eps" in the center of the page with a width of 50% of the text width, and add a caption and label for referencing. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


