<|asst|>
We use the order of operations in mathematics to ensure that there is a clear and consistent way to evaluate mathematical expressions. Without any rules, different people might interpret an expression in different ways and arrive at different answers. By using a standard order of operations, we can avoid confusion and ensure that everyone arrives at the same answer. The order of operations also ensures that more complex expressions are evaluated in a logical and organized manner. <|endoftext|>
