Write a haiku about the specific time of day - morning. The haiku should include at least three different sensory inputs, such as the sound of birds chirping, the smell of freshly brewed coffee, and the feeling of the cool breeze. In addition, the haiku must contain a reference to a specific location, such as a mountain top, a beach, or a bustling city street. Finally, the haiku must incorporate a philosophical or metaphorical theme, such as the fleeting nature of time or the beauty of impermanence.
