How can I write a Swift function to filter out all odd numbers from a given array of integers?
Here's the sample code I have so far:
func filterEvenNumbers(numbers: [Int]) -> [Int] {
 return numbers.filter { $0 % 2 == 0 }
}
But how can I modify this to return only odd numbers instead?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To modify the function to return only odd numbers, you can change the filter condition to check for numbers that have a remainder of 1 when divided by 2. Here's the updated code:
```
func filterOddNumbers(numbers: [Int]) -> [Int] {
 return numbers.filter { $0 % 2 == 1 }
}
```
This code will return an array of integers that contain only odd numbers from the input array. <|endoftext|>
