<|user|>
You are an animal behavior researcher and you want to gather information on dolphin habitat and behavior patterns. Your supervisor tells you to use Python code to retrieve the information from a website.
Using the code below, you can gather information on dolphin facts, habitats, and behaviors from the website "https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/group/dolphins-facts/". 
import requests
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
url = 'https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/group/dolphins-facts/'
response = requests.get(url)
soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, 'html.parser')
facts = []
habitats = []
behaviors = []
# Get interesting facts
fact_list = soup.find_all('li', {'class': 'facts-list__item'})
for fact in fact_list:
 facts.append(fact.text.strip())
# Get habitat information
habitat_list = soup.find_all('li', {'class': 'habitat-list__item'})
for habitat in habitat_list:
 habitats.append(habitat.text.strip())
# Get behavior patterns
behavior_list = soup.find_all('li', {'class': 'behavior-list__item'})
for behavior in behavior_list:
 behaviors.append(behavior.text.strip())
print("Interesting Facts:")
for fact in facts:
 print("- " + fact)
print("nHabitats:")
for habitat in habitats:
 print("- " + habitat)
print("nBehavior Patterns:")
for behavior in behaviors:
 print("- " + behavior)
Your task is to modify the code to only retrieve information on habitats and exclude information on behaviors and interesting facts. Can you do it?
<|end|>
