What are some common dolphin habitats and why do they prefer these areas?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Dolphins can be found in a variety of habitats including coastal areas, bays, estuaries, and open ocean. Some common dolphin habitats include warm, shallow waters with plenty of sunlight and abundant food sources such as small fish and squid. Dolphins also prefer habitats with clear water, moderate waves, and bottom topography that provides shelter and protection from predators. Additionally, dolphins migrate to warmer waters during the winter months to avoid cold temperatures. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


