How can I implement binary search in C++?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Binary search is a search algorithm that works on sorted arrays. It repeatedly divides the search interval in half until the target value is found or the search interval is empty. 

Here's an example code that implements binary search in C++:
```
#include 

int binarySearch(int arr[], int left, int right, int x) {
 while (left <= right) {
 int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

 // Check if x is present at mid
 if (arr[mid] == x)
 return mid;

 // If x greater, ignore left half 
 if (arr[mid] < x)
 left = mid + 1;

 // If x is smaller, ignore right half 
 else
 right = mid - 1;
 }

 // if we reach here, then element was not present
 return -1;
}

