Understood. Based on the criteria you provided, I recommend using a modified merge sort algorithm. First, we can split the array into two groups comprised of positive and negative numbers based on their sign. Then, for each group, we can use merge sort to sort the absolute values in non-increasing order. Finally, we can concatenate the sorted positive and negative groups together, ensuring that positive numbers come before negative numbers if they have the same absolute value. Would you like me to provide code examples for this approach? <|endoftext|>
