Sure, the time complexity of this algorithm is O(n log n) because we need to perform a modified merge sort on each group which has a time complexity of O(n log n). The space complexity is also O(n) since we need to create two additional arrays to store the positive and negative values. However, we can optimize the space complexity to O(1) by performing the sorting in-place on the original array. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
