How do I create a table in HTML with cells that change color based on user input?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To create a table in HTML with cells that change color based on user input, you can use JavaScript to manipulate the CSS of the table cells. Here's an example code snippet:
HTML:
```
|  |  |
| --- | --- |
|  |  |
```
JavaScript:
```
var cell1 = document.getElementById("cell1");
var cell2 = document.getElementById("cell2");
// Add an event listener to each cell to detect user input
cell1.addEventListener("input", function() {
 // Change the background color of the cell based on user input
 cell1.style.backgroundColor = cell1.value;
});
cell2.addEventListener("input", function() {
 // Change the background color of the cell based on user input
 cell2.style.backgroundColor = cell2.value;
});
```
In this example, the user can input a color value into each cell, and the background color of the cell will change accordingly. You can add more cells and customize the JavaScript to fit your specific needs. <|endoftext|>
