<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I can help you with that. The sorted list in ascending order would be:
12, 19, 26, 83
Here is the Excel table format for the sorted list:
| | A | B |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Original List | Sorted List |
| 2 | 12 | 12 |
| 3 | 26 | 19 |
| 4 | 83 | 26 |
| 5 | 19 | 83 |
To sort the list in Excel, you can select the cells containing the numbers you want to sort, then click on the "Data" tab, and select "Sort A to Z" from the "Sort & Filter" section. This will sort the numbers in ascending order. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain to me how the sort function works in Excel?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly. The Sort function in Excel is used to sort data within a range or table. It arranges the values in either ascending or descending order, based on a given set of criteria. When sorting data, you can choose to sort by one or more columns, and you can also specify whether to sort in ascending or descending order. In addition, you can choose whether to include or exclude header rows when sorting. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How do I sort data by multiple columns in Excel?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can sort data by multiple columns in Excel by following these steps:
1. Select the range of data that you want to sort.
2. Click the "Data" tab in the Ribbon.
3. Click the "Sort" button in the "Sort & Filter" group.
4. In the "Sort" dialog box, select the first column that you want to sort by from the "Sort by" drop-down list.
5. Choose the sort order (ascending or descending) for the first column.
6. Click the "Add Level" button to add another column to sort by.
7. Select the second column that you want to sort by from the "Then by" drop-down list.
8. Choose the sort order (ascending or descending) for the second column.
9. Repeat steps 6-8 for any additional columns that you want to sort by.
10. Click the "OK" button to sort the data by the selected columns. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Is there a way to automatically update the sorted list when new data is added to the original list in Excel?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, there is a way to automatically update the sorted list in Excel when new data is added to the original list. This can be done using the Excel Table feature. Here are the steps to create an Excel Table and automatically update the sorted list:
1. Select the range of data that you want to sort.
2. Click the "Insert" tab in the Ribbon.
3. Click the "Table" button in the "Tables" group.
4. In the "Create Table" dialog box, make sure the range of data is correct and that the "My table has headers" option is checked.
5. Click the "OK" button to create the table.
6. With the table selected, click the "Design" tab in the Ribbon.
7. In the "Properties" group, click the "Table Name" text box and give the table a name.
8. Click the "Add" button in the "Columns" group to add a new column to the table for the sorted list.
9. In the first cell of the new column, enter the formula "=SORT(TableName[Original List])", where "TableName" is the name you gave to your table and "Original List" is the header of the column containing the original list of numbers.
10. Press Enter to apply the formula to the cell.
11. The sorted list will now be automatically updated whenever new data is added to the original list. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
