5. Click the "OK" button to sort the names alphabetically.

If you want to sort the names by last name instead of first name, you can use a formula to extract the last name from each name and sort the list based on that. Here's how:
1. Insert a new column next to the column containing the names.
2. In the first cell of the new column, enter the formula "=RIGHT(A1,LEN(A1)-FIND(" ",A1))", where "A1" is the cell containing the name. This formula extracts the last name from the name.
3. Copy the formula down the entire column to apply it to all cells in the column.
4. Select the range of cells containing both columns (the original column with full names and the new column with last names only).
5. Click the "Data" tab in the Ribbon.
6. Click the "Sort" button in the "Sort & Filter" group.
7. In the "Sort" dialog box, select the column containing the last names from the "Sort by" drop-down list.
8. Choose the sort order (ascending or descending) for the last names.
