I have a list of famous writers and their birth and death dates in an Excel table format as shown below:
| Writer | Birth Year | Death Year |
|----------------|------------|------------|
| William Shakespeare | 1564 | 1616 |
| Jane Austen | 1775 | 1817 |
| Ernest Hemingway | 1899 | 1961 |
Based on this data, I want to know:
How long did William Shakespeare live?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
William Shakespeare was born in 1564 and died in 1616. To calculate how long he lived, we can subtract his birth year from his death year: 
1616 - 1564 = 52
William Shakespeare lived for 52 years. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Thanks for your answer! Now, can you tell me which writer on the list had the shortest lifespan?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly! To determine the writer with the shortest lifespan, we need to calculate the number of years they lived by subtracting their birth year from their death year. 

| Writer | Birth Year | Death Year | Lifespan |
|----------------|------------|------------|----------|
| William Shakespeare | 1564 | 1616 | 52 |
| Jane Austen | 1775 | 1817 | 42 |
| Ernest Hemingway | 1899 | 1961 | 62 |

As shown in the table, Jane Austen had the shortest lifespan of 42 years. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
