<|asst|>
AI (Artificial Intelligence) refers to the broad field of technology that involves creating machines or systems that can perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, such as visual perception, speech recognition, decision-making, and natural language processing. Machine Learning (ML) is a specific subset of AI that involves using algorithms and statistical models to enable machines to learn from data and improve their performance over time without being explicitly programmed.
