 return 0;
}
I'm not sure how to modify it to incorporate the translation of "The dog is barking loudly". Any suggestions?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can modify the code to add a new key-value pair for the English translation and then output the entire JSON object with all four translations. Here's an example:
```
#include 
#include 
int main()
{
 Json::Value translation;
 translation["English"] = "The dog is barking loudly";
 translation["Spanish"] = "El perro está ladrando fuerte";
 translation["French"] = "Le chien aboie bruyamment";
 translation["German"] = "Der Hund bellt laut";
