<|user|>
How can we prove that the sum of angles in a triangle is always 180 degrees?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
One way to prove this is by drawing a line parallel to one of the sides of the triangle, creating two smaller triangles. Then, using the fact that the sum of angles in a straight line is 180 degrees and the corresponding angles of parallel lines are equal, we can show that the sum of angles in the original triangle is also 180 degrees. <|endoftext|>
