<|user|>
Can you solve this riddle about organizing and displaying poems on a webpage? I have a collection of poems with different attributes such as author, genre, and theme. I want to store them in a SQL database. How can I create a database to organize the poems in such a way that I can retrieve all the poems that have a spring theme and display them on a webpage with their titles and authors? And can you help me sort them in alphabetical order based on the author's last name? Remember, every attribute of a poem should be stored in the database.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I can help you with that. Here's how you can create a SQL database to organize your poems:
1. Create a table called "poems" with the following columns: 
- poem_id (primary key)
- title
- author_first_name
- author_last_name
- genre
- theme
2. Insert all your poems into the "poems" table with their corresponding attributes.
3. To retrieve all the poems that have a spring theme, you can use the following SQL query: 
```
SELECT title, author_last_name FROM poems WHERE theme='spring'
```
This will return a list of all the titles and authors of the poems that have a spring theme.
4. To sort the results in alphabetical order based on the author's last name, you can add the following line to the SQL query: 
```
ORDER BY author_last_name ASC
```
This will sort the results in ascending order based on the author's last name.
5. Once you have the results, you can display them on a webpage using your preferred programming language and web development tools. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That's great! But what if I want to add a new attribute to my poems, such as the year it was written? Do I have to create a new table or can I modify the existing table?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To add a new attribute to your poems, such as the year it was written, you can simply add a new column to your existing "poems" table. You can do this using the ALTER TABLE statement in SQL. Here's an example of how you can add a "year_written" column to your "poems" table:
```
ALTER TABLE poems ADD COLUMN year_written INTEGER;
```
This will add a new column called "year_written" to your "poems" table, which is of type INTEGER. Once you've added the new column, you can update your existing rows with the year each poem was written. And when you want to retrieve the year information of each poem, you can simply add the "year_written" column to your SELECT statement. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


