How does deep learning differ from traditional machine learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Deep learning is a subset of machine learning that uses artificial neural networks with multiple layers to extract hierarchical features from data. Traditional machine learning algorithms often require manual feature engineering, where domain experts select and extract relevant features from the data. In contrast, deep learning models can automatically learn features from raw data by iteratively applying non-linear transformations to the input. This makes deep learning highly effective for tasks such as image recognition, speech recognition, and natural language processing, where the underlying patterns and relationships may be complex and difficult to capture using traditional methods. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
