<|end|>
<|asst|>
Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence that involves training algorithms to make predictions or decisions based on data. It can be supervised, unsupervised, or semi-supervised. In contrast, deep learning is a specific type of machine learning that utilizes deep neural networks to perform tasks such as image or speech recognition. Deep learning is inspired by the structure and function of the human brain, with nodes (neurons) organized in layers that process information.
Both machine learning and deep learning are used in various applications of artificial intelligence, including natural language processing, computer vision, and robotics. Machine learning can be used for tasks such as spam filtering, recommendation systems, and fraud detection. Deep learning, on the other hand, excels at complex tasks such as object recognition in images and speech-to-text conversion. <|endoftext|>
