```
package main
import (
 "fmt"
 "github.com/kniren/gota/dataframe"
)
func main() {
 // Load the CSV file.
 titanicData := dataframe.ReadCSV("titanic.csv")
 
 // Calculate summary statistics for the age column.
 summary := titanicData.Col("age").Summary()
 
 // Print the summary statistics.
 fmt.Println(summary)
}
```
This code loads a Titanic passenger dataset from a CSV file and uses the `Col()` method to extract the `age` column. It then calls the `Summary()` method to calculate summary statistics for the column, including the minimum value, the maximum value, the mean, the median, and more. Finally, it prints out the summary statistics using the `fmt` package. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
