<|asst|>
To create a website for a new restaurant that has a menu and reservation system, along with an online ordering system, you can use Java in conjunction with popular web frameworks like Spring or Struts. Here's a sample code snippet for creating a menu page using Spring:
```
@Controller
public class MenuController {
 @RequestMapping("/menu")
 public String showMenu(Model model) {
 List menuItems = getMenuItems(); // retrieve menu items from database or other source
 model.addAttribute("menuItems", menuItems);
 return "menu";
 }
 @RequestMapping("/order")
 public String orderItem(@RequestParam("itemId") int itemId, Model model) {
 MenuItem item = getItemById(itemId); // retrieve item by ID from database or other source
 model.addAttribute("item", item);
 return "order";
 }
 @PostMapping("/confirmOrder")
 public String confirmOrder(@ModelAttribute("order") Order order) {
 // process order and send confirmation to customer
 return "orderConfirmation";
 }
}
```
This code defines a controller for the menu page, which retrieves menu items from a data source and passes them to the view. It also includes methods for ordering an item and confirming the order.
