Can you create an Excel table that showcases the deep bond of companionship between individuals based on mutual trust, respect, and support, and culminates in a conclusion featuring the keyword "companionship"? The table should include data such as names, shared experiences, level of trust and respect, and support given/received. Additionally, please include Excel VBA code to automatically calculate the overall level of companionship based on the data entered.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Here's an example Excel table that showcases the deep bond of companionship between individuals based on mutual trust, respect, and support:
| Name 1 | Name 2 | Shared Experiences | Level of Trust | Level of Respect | Support Given | Support Received | Overall Companionship Level |
|--------|--------|--------------------|----------------|------------------|---------------|-----------------|------------------------------|
| John | Mary | Traveling together | 9/10 | 8/10 | Emotional | Financial | 8.5/10 |
| Alex | Sarah | Working on a project | 7/10 | 9/10 | Professional | Emotional | 8/10 |
| David | Lisa | Childhood friends | 10/10 | 10/10 | Financial | Professional | 10/10 |
And here's the VBA code to automatically calculate the overall level of companionship based on the data entered:
```
Private Sub Worksheet_Change(ByVal Target As Range)
 If Not Intersect(Target, Range("D2:F4")) Is Nothing Then
 Dim trust As Double
 Dim respect As Double
 Dim support As Double
 Dim companionship As Double
 
 trust = (Range("D" & Target.Row) + Range("E" & Target.Row)) / 2
 respect = Range("F" & Target.Row)
 support = (Range("G" & Target.Row) + Range("H" & Target.Row)) / 2
 
 companionship = (trust + respect + support) / 3
 Range("I" & Target.Row) = companionship
 End If
End Sub
```
This code will automatically calculate the overall companionship level whenever there's a change in the trust, respect, or support columns for any of the rows. The companionship level is calculated as the average of the three components. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
