Phagocytes are another key part of the immune system, which engulf and digest foreign particles such as bacteria and viruses. Additionally, there are many different types of cytokines and chemokines, which are signaling molecules that help coordinate the immune response. Overall, the immune system is a complex and sophisticated defense mechanism that plays a crucial role in protecting the body from infection and disease. <|endoftext|>
