How can I use Swift to design an interactive virtual reality portfolio showcase using the data in my excel table? What Swift functions or code can I use to enhance the user experience and interactivity of the showcase?
As for using the excel table, I suggest converting it to a CSV file and parsing the data in Swift. You can use the following code to parse a CSV file in Swift:
```
func parseCSV(contentsOfURL: NSURL, encoding: NSStringEncoding, error: NSErrorPointer) -> [[String]]? {
 guard let contents = try? String(contentsOf: contentsOfURL as URL, encoding: encoding) else {
 return nil
 }
 
 var lines: [[String]] = []
 let rows = contents.components(separatedBy: NSCharacterSet.newlines) as [String]
 for row in rows {
 let columns = row.components(separatedBy: ",")
 lines.append(columns)
 }
 
 return lines
}
```
Once you have parsed the data, you can use it to populate your virtual reality showcase. As for enhancing the interactivity and user experience, you can use Swift's SceneKit framework to create 3D models of your projects and allow users to interact with them in a virtual environment. You can also use Core Animation to create dynamic animations and transitions within the showcase.
