<|user|>
What is the PHP code to calculate the average age of a list of individuals? Here's an example list:
$individuals = array(
 array("name" => "Person 1", "age" => 12),
 array("name" => "Person 2", "age" => 57),
 array("name" => "Person 3", "age" => 22)
);
What is the PHP code that can be used to compute the average age of this list?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the PHP code to calculate the average age of a list of individuals:
```
$individuals = array(
 array("name" => "Person 1", "age" => 12),
 array("name" => "Person 2", "age" => 57),
 array("name" => "Person 3", "age" => 22)
);
$sum = 0;
$count = count($individuals);
foreach ($individuals as $person) {
 $sum += $person['age'];
}
$average = $sum / $count;
echo "The average age is: " . $average;
```
This code initializes the sum of ages to zero and counts the number of individuals in the list. It then loops through each individual and adds their age to the sum. Finally, it calculates the average age by dividing the sum by the count and outputs the result. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain the difference between procedural and object-oriented programming?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Procedural programming is a programming paradigm that involves dividing a program into smaller subroutines or procedures. These procedures take input, process it, and produce output. In procedural programming, the focus is on performing tasks or operations on data. On the other hand, object-oriented programming (OOP) is a programming paradigm that focuses on creating objects that contain both data and behavior. Objects are instances of classes, which are templates for creating objects with similar characteristics. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What is encapsulation in object-oriented programming?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Encapsulation is one of the fundamental principles of object-oriented programming. It refers to the idea of bundling data and behavior together into a single unit called a class. The data and behavior within a class are hidden from outside access and can only be accessed through methods that have been exposed by the class. This provides a way to control access to the data and behavior within an object and prevents external code from interfering with the internal workings of the object. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How does inheritance work in object-oriented programming?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Inheritance is another important concept in object-oriented programming. It allows a new class to be defined based on an existing class, inheriting all of its properties and behaviors. The new class is called the derived class or subclass, and the existing class is called the base class or superclass. The derived class can then add its own unique features while still retaining the characteristics of the base class. This saves time on coding and makes code reuse possible. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What is polymorphism in object-oriented programming?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Polymorphism is the ability of objects to take on different forms or behaviors depending on the context in which they are used. In object-oriented programming, this means that objects of different classes can be treated as if they are of the same class, allowing them to be used interchangeably. Polymorphism is achieved through two mechanisms: inheritance and interfaces. Inheritance allows a derived class to inherit properties and behaviors from its base class, while interfaces specify a set of methods that must be implemented by any class that implements the interface. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


