<|end|>
<|asst|>
While modern technology has certainly impacted daily life in Kyoto, the city has managed to preserve its traditional culture and way of life. Many artisans continue to practice traditional crafts and perform ancient rituals, while also incorporating modern techniques and materials. Additionally, Kyoto has become a hub for innovation in sustainable technologies, demonstrating a balance between modernity and tradition. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some popular festivals celebrated in Kyoto? Can you tell me a little bit about their significance and what visitors can expect?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Kyoto is known for its many colorful and vibrant festivals throughout the year. Some popular festivals include the Gion Matsuri in July, which features a massive parade of floats and attracts over 1 million visitors, and the Aoi Matsuri in May, which celebrates the harvest season with a procession of people dressed in traditional court attire. Visitors can expect to see traditional Japanese music and dance performances, elaborate costumes, and plenty of delicious food and drink during these festivals. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


