<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, the code can be modified to allow users to input their own ingredients. One way to do this would be to add a new function that prompts the user to enter information about their custom ingredients, such as the weight, protein content, carbohydrate content, and fat content. The function could then add this information to the nutrient database and use it in the calculation of the macronutrient breakdown. Another option would be to prompt the user to enter their custom ingredients in JSON format along with their preferences, and modify the `filterNutrientData` function to include the custom ingredients in the filtered data. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


