3. Increase the size of the matrix to 7x7 or higher, or increase the range of integers used in the matrix.
4. Introduce more complex relationships between the elements in the matrix, such as diagonal or anti-diagonal sums, or even non-linear relationships like Fibonacci numbers.
5. Consider incorporating time constraints or penalties if the player takes too long to solve the puzzle.

