<|user|>
How can I use PHP to correct the sentence "The foxes were ran out of the woods" and identify the parts of speech of each word in the original sentence based on the following formula for identifying parts of speech: 
Noun: (NN|NNS|NNP|NNPS)
Verb: (VB|VBD|VBG|VBN|VBP|VBZ)
Adjective: (JJ|JJR|JJS)
Adverb: (RB|RBR|RBS)
Pronoun: (PRP|PRP$|WP|WP$)
Preposition: (IN)
Conjunction: (CC)
Interjection: (UH) 
Here is the PHP code I have tried so far:
$sentence = "The foxes were ran out of the woods";
$tags = pos_tag(word_tokenize($sentence));
foreach ($tags as $tag) {
 $word = $tag[0];
 $pos = $tag[1];
 switch ($pos) {
 case 'NN':
 case 'NNS':
 case 'NNP':
 case 'NNPS':
 echo $word . " is a noun. ";
 break;
 case 'VB':
 case 'VBD':
 case 'VBG':
 case 'VBN':
 case 'VBP':
 case 'VBZ':
 echo $word . " is a verb. ";
 break;
 case 'JJ':
 case 'JJR':
 case 'JJS':
 echo $word . " is an adjective. ";
 break;
 case 'RB':
 case 'RBR':
 case 'RBS':
 echo $word . " is an adverb. ";
 break;
 case 'PRP':
 case 'PRP$':
 case 'WP':
 case 'WP$':
 echo $word . " is a pronoun. ";
 break;
 case 'IN':
 echo $word . " is a preposition. ";
 break;
 case 'CC':
 echo $word . " is a conjunction. ";
 break;
 case 'UH':
 echo $word . " is an interjection. ";
 break;
 default:
 echo $word . " is not recognized. ";
 break;
 }
}
How can I modify this code to correct the sentence and output the corrected sentence with the identified parts of speech for each word?
